  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "Medium composition from PMC6373973 (see GrowthDB record).",
  "doi": "",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6373973/",
  "notes": "Full recipe recovered from the primary literature: base medium 'Defined synthetic anaerobic-digestion (biogas) glucose-cellulose medium, with glucose+cellulose replaced by 14.6% (v/v) ethanol as the sole main carbon/energy source (\"ethanol medium\")' (Basic medium composition defined in Bensmann A, Hanke-Rauschenbach R, Heyer R, Kohrs F, Benndorf D, Kausmann R, et al. Diagnostic concept for dynamically operated biogas production plants. Renewable Energy. 2016;96:479-489. DOI:10.1016/j.renene.2016",
  "verification": "paper-verified (recipe recovered from primary literature)",
  "verification_note": "Could NOT access full medium composition. The accessible article text confirms only ethanol (14.6% v/v) as the main carbon source of an anaerobic-digestion (biogas reactor) enrichment culture; salts, nitrogen source, buffer, vitamins, and trace elements are relegated to supplementary S6 Text (and reference [31]) and were not retrievable. Oxygen = anaerobic is supported by the anaerobic-digestion/b",
  "recipe_evidence": "RedCom S6 Text (this paper): 'For the cultivation on ethanol performed in this study, we used biomass from an enrichment that was run 520 days on glucose-cellulose medium [Kohrs et al.]. As main carbon sources, glucose and cellulose were replaced by 14.6% (v/v) ethanol; all other medium components were left the same.' Kohrs et al. 2017 Anaerobe: 'The basic composition of the medium is described by Bensmann et al. [20] with the following exception: meat extract, yeast extract, and peptone were replaced by 11.5 g L-1 glucose and 34.4 g L-1 cellulose as carbon source to exclude any undefined comp",
  "recipe_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "Defined synthetic anaerobic-digestion (biogas) glucose-cellulose medium, with glucose+cellulose replaced by 14.6% (v/v) ethanol as the sole main carbon/energy source (\"ethanol medium\")",
  "base_medium_reference": "Basic medium composition defined in Bensmann A, Hanke-Rauschenbach R, Heyer R, Kohrs F, Benndorf D, Kausmann R, et al. Diagnostic concept for dynamically operated biogas production plants. Renewable Energy. 2016;96:479-489. DOI:10.1016/j.renene.2016.04.098. Medium as used (glucose+cellulose replaced by ethanol) described in Koch et al. RedCom, PLoS Comput Biol 2019;15(2):e1006759 S6 Text (this paper), which references Kohrs F, Heyer R, Bissinger T, Kottler R, Schallert K, Puttker S, et al. Proteotyping of laboratory-scale biogas plants reveals multiple steady-states in community composition. Anaerobe. 2017;46:56-68. DOI:10.1016/j.anaerobe.2017.02.005; PMID:28189830. Full quantitative recipe (Tables 7-9) recovered from the open-access PhD dissertation of F. Kohrs (Otto-von-Guericke-Universitaet Magdeburg), MPG pure item_3344958, https://pure.mpg.de/rest/items/item_3344958_5/component/file_3363606/content",
